Rolling linux apps 2.1.11
-------------------------------------------

Universal multi-OEM package release (Canonical review 2026-11):

* One universal package now ships every OEM variant: the rolling_helper
  binaries from all helper_set/<project>_<oem>/ directories and the ini
  templates from all config_set/ and flash_set/ sets.  /usr/bin/rolling_helper
  dispatches on the machine vendor (DMI) at runtime and fails loudly on an
  unknown vendor.
* The ini configuration files are no longer dpkg conffiles: they ship as
  templates under /usr/share/linux-apps/{config_set,flash_set}/ and are
  seeded into /etc/rolling/config_file/ by seed_config.sh -- best-effort
  from the postinst, and again at each boot by the rolling_seed_config.service
  oneshot while the config is missing.  Seeding never overwrites an existing
  file, so operator edits survive upgrades; purge removes them together with
  /etc/rolling.
* Runtime data lives in /usr/share/linux-apps (FHS /usr/share/<package>
  naming); third-party libraries are resolved from the system via the
  declared package dependencies (no vendor bundling, no RUNPATH
  rewriting at packaging time).
* Manual pages ship for the four services and the two ini
  configuration files: rolling_config(8), rolling_flash(8),
  rolling_helper(8), rolling_ma(8), rwwwanConfig.ini(5),
  FwUpdate.ini(5) (Debian Policy 12.1).
* preinst migrates operator-edited ini files from the legacy
  /etc/opt/rolling layout before unpack.
* The package declares Breaks/Conflicts/Replaces against the old per-OEM
  packages (linux-apps-<platform>-<project>-<oem> (<< 2.1.11)) so dpkg
  replaces them automatically on upgrade.

Rolling linux apps 1.0.0
-------------------------------------------

This is a new stable release of Rolling Linux services.  Notable changes include:

* systemd integration
* flash service
* config service
* ma service
* helper service
